1. `shadowbonk.html:99-100` — deleted the second `const picks=[];const pool=POOL.slice();` in `pick3()` (redeclaration was a SyntaxError that killed the whole script).
2. `shadowbonk.html:84` — appended `});` to close the keydown arrow so `startGame()` and everything after it are top-level again (was swallowing the rest of the script into an unclosed listener).
3. `shadowbonk.html:95,108,116,231-236,240-242` — defined `const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),gid=$;` after `const W=2800,H=2000;`.
